section(2,'Problem Statement, Use Case & Track 3 Alignment')
add('A production runbook says `max_retries=3`, an older PR says `4`, and a later Slack hotfix sets `5`. A staging document is newer still but applies to a different environment. An operations assistant must establish the requested entity and production scope, follow deployment evidence, compare dates, cite actual observations, and flag the stale page. An incident request additionally requires discovering its service, timestamps or payload before calculating a cost. If an explicitly required database server is unplugged, answering from another silo violates the request. This is the Stale-Doc Trap in multilingual engineering teams.')
add('The [official hackathon Track 3 problem list](https://hackathon.lexsi.ai/#tracks), verified during this documentation pass, places our six areas at official items 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 and 9. The original `/tracks` URL returned 404; the homepage contains the track details. The following mapping is an implementation assessment, not an assertion that every deployment goal was achieved.')
add(table(['Official item / area','What DriftGuard implements','Evidence and boundary'],[
['1 · Reliable tool calling','Live model-generated XML/JSON calls, strict schemas, ordering and tool feedback','AgentTune-backed multi-turn episodes; all 500 final selected-GRPO holdout finals format-valid'],
['2 · Efficient trajectories','Measured discovery-oracle lengths and success-gated excess-step penalties','Tool counts, redundancy and outcome reported separately; fewer calls can also omit required evidence'],
['4 · Retrieval-augmented generation','Model decides queries and follows runbook hints; filters staging and sibling records','Up to three query-ranked records; complete-chain compliance remains a weakness'],
['5 · Synthetic multi-hop data','Facts-first histories and oracle trajectories with disjoint phase case pools','Frozen datasets and manifests; synthetic, not harvested real enterprise documents'],
['6 · Data/database agents','Read-only SQLite incident discovery plus deterministic time/conversion/math','Exact scalar scoring and required utility-chain gate'],
['9 · Reward-hacking defences','Three transparent reward modes, adversarial policies, positive anchors','Original loopholes retained as counterexamples; no claim of an ungameable reward']]))
add('A small model permits inference within an organization-controlled workstation or VPC, keeping private PR content, Slack incidents and production schemas inside that boundary when all connectors and logging are also controlled. The experiment uses synthetic evidence, so it does not itself demonstrate deployment on private company data. Nine server interfaces and native-script examples support the Indian-language use case; correctness is still measured per language rather than assumed from model branding. Local deployment feasibility was measured on an RTX 2070 8GB with a v1 NF4 adapter; final v2 GRPO accuracy was measured on L40S in BF16. Base/model-card license metadata identifies a noncommercial license; enterprise commercial deployment requires checking the applicable terms rather than assuming unrestricted use.')
section(3,'Training & Evaluation Environment Architecture — How the World Works')
add('The original design lives in `src/world_generator.py`, `src/real_repo_world.py`, `src/mcp_env.py` and `src/mcp_adapter.py`. Versioned v2 generation is implemented by `src/v2_world.py`, `src/v2_tasks.py`, `src/v2_oracle.py`, `src/v2_dataset.py` and `src/v2_env.py`; copied runtime modules under `src_v2/`, `src_v2_1/` and `src_v2_2/` isolate subsequent experiments from legacy code. The final runtime validates schema version 2 and binds all input paths to `data_v2/`.')
add('Each episode creates its own `sqlite3.connect(":memory:")` connection, inserts a deterministic snapshot, commits initialization, then enables `PRAGMA query_only=ON` and an SQLite authorizer. The agent may read only `microservices` and `production_incidents`; the three search collections also have snapshot tables but are accessed through their tools. SQL must start with SELECT, rows are capped at 32, and a progress handler bounds execution. Failures return an error object for feedback. This is connection-per-episode isolation, not a measured sub-millisecond parallel transaction service. `sql_dump()` exports trusted DDL/INSERT snapshots; PostgreSQL execution was not benchmarked. Local rollouts call Python functions in-process; an optional FastMCP wrapper exposes the same router, not nine separately deployed production integrations.')
