add('Conversion factors are kg→lb = 2.2046226218487757, decimal GB→MiB = 1e9/2^20, and hours→minutes = 60, with reverse conversions supported. Safe AST arithmetic accepts bounded numeric +, −, ×, ÷ and a restricted `round(arithmetic, places)` wrapper (0–6 places); it does not evaluate arbitrary Python. Weather and calendar return deterministic distractor outputs, never live forecasts or real meetings.')
add('### Protocol and task semantics\n\nEvery assistant turn contains exactly one XML wrapper around strict JSON. Tool observations are appended as user-role `Tool result:` messages because this chat-template integration does not use a native function-call transport. Explanations outside the wrapper or invalid response contracts fail parsing. Numeric normalization equates numeric strings and finite numeric scalars; multi-number dumps do not equal a single gold value.')
add('''```xml
<tool_call>{"server":"notion-mcp","tool":"search_notion","arguments":{"query":"litellm-router-proxy max_retries"}}</tool_call>
<final_answer>{"status":"conflict_resolved","value":12,"cites":["NOTION-V2-OSS-007","SLACK-V2-OSS-007"],"stale_source":"NOTION-V2-OSS-007"}</final_answer>
```

This final-answer example is the recorded scalar-correct but chain-incomplete trace discussed in Section 8; it is not a fully compliant gold answer. `answered` requires `stale_source=null`; `conflict_resolved` identifies an outdated page; `abstain` requires `value=null`. Evidence IDs enter the retrieved set only when actually returned by a tool observation.''')
