add('Search tokenizes Unicode word/hyphen tokens, strips a multilingual generic stopword set, filters explicit parameter tokens, adds service/parameter overlap bonuses and breaks ties by timestamp and stable JSON. For a recognized entity it retains at most two own-entity records plus sibling results to fill three slots. Newer `[STAGING-ONLY]` records commonly rank first above `[PROD]`; this is not an invariant for every query, and filtering comes from record scope, not a guaranteed ordering. Selection is query-based and does not consult task gold labels. Both GitHub and Slack remain active for ordinary audits; about 30% of conflict case construction adds cross-channel override histories. The system prompt supplies protocol, schemas and task rules, but user prompts do not name a required deployment tool or utility sequence. Database-only abstention prompts intentionally state their source requirement.')
