section(4,'Data Curation, Anti-Leakage & the v1 → v2 Benchmark Evolution')
add('All ground truth, timestamps, configuration histories and incident fields are generated from structured Python facts before text rendering. No LLM invented the gold facts. The train world has seed 42, 60 services, 80 incidents and 320 semantic cases: 300 allocated plus 20 reserved; synthetic holdout uses seed 99 and a separate namespace. Training phases share the broader enterprise namespace but have disjoint case IDs, service-parameter pairs and incident IDs. Thus “zero leakage” here means those tested boundaries, not proof that no statistical shortcut exists, no shared service appears across train phases, or no numeric values recur. The allowed domain intervals are shared, but configuration integer candidates are partitioned by value modulo 3: train residue 1, synthetic residue 2, OSS-style residue 0. That makes configuration-value vocabularies split-disjoint within those intervals; incident rates, converted quantities and computed outcomes are not guaranteed globally disjoint. This artificial residue split is itself a benchmark limitation.')
